WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:08.230
VoxTexto turns audio and video files into text to help you
organize lectures, interviews, meetings and other
recordings.

2
00:00:09.066 --> 00:00:17.366
Speech recognition runs on your computer. Follow the
process in the interface and receive a Word document for
further review.

3
00:00:18.204 --> 00:00:24.126
To get started, select files, choose a folder or drag your
recordings into the upload area.

4
00:00:24.964 --> 00:00:33.107
The queue shows each file name, format, duration and size,
so you can check what will be processed before starting.

5
00:00:33.944 --> 00:00:42.767
Files are transcribed in sequence, with individual status
and processing times. The dedicated panel helps you track
the current file.

6
00:00:43.604 --> 00:00:51.153
You can pause between files or cancel processing. The time
required depends on the recording and computer
performance.

7
00:00:51.990 --> 00:01:00.364
When transcription finishes, the text is displayed on
screen. A Word document is generated automatically and can
be downloaded with one click.

8
00:01:01.201 --> 00:01:09.624
Check the recognized content and make any adjustments you
need. This demonstration shows a short recording actually
transcribed by the application.

9
00:01:10.461 --> 00:01:19.782
History keeps records linked to your account. Search for a
recording, filter results and check the details of each
transcription.

10
00:01:20.619 --> 00:01:28.544
Generated texts and documents remain available for
consultation. The application includes sign-in and user
and administrator roles.

11
00:01:29.381 --> 00:01:38.434
Choose Dark, Light or HUD themes and adjust interface
preferences. Statistics help you monitor your account
results.

12
00:01:39.272 --> 00:01:48.507
VoxTexto brings selection, transcription, history and
export together in one workflow. Explore the project and
turn your recordings into documents.
